  "title": "Table per Concrete Type (TPC)",
  "description": "Learn TPC strategy with separate tables for each concrete type.",
  "order": 4,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "tags": ["ef-core", "tpc", "inheritance", "concrete"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Table per Concrete Type (TPC)** maps each concrete (non-abstract) type to its own table. Each table includes both base properties and type-specific properties."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "TPC Characteristics"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "One table per concrete type",
          "No base table and no discriminator",
          "Base columns duplicated in every concrete table",
          "Polymorphic queries use UNION ALL"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
      "data": {
        "id": "tpc-diagram",
        "caption": "TPC concrete table structure",
        "definition": "graph TD\n    A[Cat Table] --> B[Id, Name, Lives]\n    C[Dog Table] --> D[Id, Name, IsGoodBoy]"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "When to Use TPC"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "You want to avoid JOINs and prefer independent tables",
          "Polymorphic queries are rare",
          "Duplicating base columns is acceptable"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "When to Avoid TPC"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "You need strict normalized design",
          "Polymorphic queries are frequent",
          "You rely on shared base-type reporting"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "Separate tables for each concrete type",
          "No base table, no discriminator",
          "Base columns duplicated",
          "UNION ALL for polymorphic queries"
        ],
        "takeaway": "Continue to learn about migrations."
      }
    }
  ],
  "relatedLessons": ["ef-core-table-per-type-tpt", "migrations-in-entity-framework-core"],
